{"id": "66552b1b-b39c-4575-84ff-d9f10be4977d", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll audit CloudTrail in us-east-1. That means looking at the trail configuration (scope, event selectors, logging status) and checking whether log delivery to S3 and CloudWatch Logs is working.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_dzm98DkZnfsn2eVG6FxfLS", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "cloudtrail-coverage-audit", "agent_type": "generic", "preloaded_skills": ["investigating-infrastructure-changes", "searching-logs", "verifying-with-docs"], "prompt": "{
  "task": "Audit CloudTrail coverage and log delivery health for the us-east-1 Region only.",
  "context": "User asks: 'Is anything in us-east-1 not being logged, and are the logs actually being delivered?' This is a read-only configuration audit, not a root-cause hunt. Do not mutate anything. Note: use_aws CloudTrail calls may be blocked; if so, use the CloudTrail lookup tool from the preloaded skill and other read-only routes (e.g. S3 head/list, CloudWatch Logs describe, CloudWatch metrics, CloudFormation) to infer what you can, and clearly state what could not be verified.",
  "resources": ["AWS account 012345678901", "Region us-east-1"],
  "timeframe": "Current state, plus the last 7 days for delivery evidence (now is 2026-11-19T15:38:30Z)",
  "criteria": "1) Coverage: list every trail visible in us-east-1 (including multi-Region and organization trails whose home Region may differ but which cover us-east-1) and any CloudTrail Lake event data stores. For each: IsLogging, IsMultiRegionTrail, IsOrganizationTrail, IncludeGlobalServiceEvents, management event selectors (ReadWriteType, excluded sources), advanced/data event selectors (S3 object-level, Lambda, DynamoDB etc.), Insights, log file validation, KMS encryption. Identify gaps: no trail at all, trails stopped, read-only or write-only management events, no data events for S3 buckets/Lambda functions/DynamoDB tables that exist in us-east-1 (flag notable ones, e.g. buckets), excluded event sources (KMS, RDS Data API). 2) Delivery: from trail status, check LatestDeliveryTime, LatestDeliveryError, LatestNotificationError, LatestCloudWatchLogsDeliveryTime/Error, LatestDigestDeliveryTime/Error, StartLoggingTime/StopLoggingTime. Verify the destination S3 bucket exists, has a bucket policy allowing cloudtrail.amazonaws.com (if readable), and that recent log objects (under AWSLogs/<account>/CloudTrail/us-east-1/ for the last day or two) are actually present. Verify the CloudWatch Logs group and role if configured. Flag staleness (e.g. last delivery > ~1 hour old) or errors. Return a concise findings summary: what is covered, what gaps exist, delivery health per trail, and prioritized recommendations."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Audit CloudTrail trails and log delivery in us-east-1"}], "created_at": null}

